      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are correct that prioritizing the prevention of harm and upholding the dignity of marginalized groups is increasingly becoming the dominant approach in the industry. Many major platforms and regulatory bodies now lean heavily against the joke defense, utilizing specific indicators like the presence of hate tropes or coordinated networks to flag even what appears to be satire. Implementing a \"harm-first\" methodology not only aligns with growing legal risks and best practices but also offers a more robust and defensible standard than waiting for suffering to occur before taking action. Consequently, prioritizing the protection of powerful or protected groups is widely considered the more socially responsible and future-proof strategy for modern social media governance.",
